\subsection*{1. Capsule Lineage Ordering Relation}

A Codex Capsule is defined as:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{C}
= (\mathcal{M}, H_{\mathrm{commit}}, \Gamma),
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{M}$ is the manuscript payload,
$H_{\mathrm{commit}}$ the cryptographic commitment,
and $\Gamma$ the glyph-seal semantic layer.

We define a lineage ordering relation $\prec$ such that:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{C}_i \prec \mathcal{C}_j
\quad \Longleftrightarrow \quad
\text{$\mathcal{C}_j$ depends on, extends, or resonates with $\mathcal{C}_i$}.
\end{equation}

This relation is:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{transitive}:  
    $\mathcal{C}_i \prec \mathcal{C}_j$ and 
    $\mathcal{C}_j \prec \mathcal{C}_k$
    imply $\mathcal{C}_i \prec \mathcal{C}_k$,
    \item \textbf{antisymmetric}:  
    $\mathcal{C}_i \prec \mathcal{C}_j$ and 
    $\mathcal{C}_j \prec \mathcal{C}_i$
    imply $\mathcal{C}_i = \mathcal{C}_j$,
    \item \textbf{non-total}:  
    some capsules are incomparable.
\end{itemize}

Thus, capsule lineage forms a \emph{partially ordered set (poset)}.

\subsection*{2. Lineage Invariants}

Each capsule $\mathcal{C}_i$ carries an invariant signature:
\begin{equation}
I(\mathcal{C}_i)
= \mathrm{SHA256}(\mathcal{M}_i \parallel \Gamma_i),
\end{equation}
which must satisfy:
\begin{equation}
I(\mathcal{C}_i) \neq I(\mathcal{C}_j)
\quad \text{for all } i \neq j.
\end{equation}

Lineage invariants ensure:
\begin{itemize}
    \item uniqueness,
    \item non-collision,
    \item semantic isolation,
    \item resonance consistency.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{3. Resonance Operator}

We define the capsule resonance operator $\mathcal{R}$:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{C}_i, \mathcal{C}_j)
= \Gamma_i \otimes \Gamma_j,
\end{equation}
where $\otimes$ is the glyph-seal tensor product.

Resonance exists if:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{C}_i, \mathcal{C}_j) \neq 0.
\end{equation}

Capsule lineage is resonance-driven:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{C}_i \prec \mathcal{C}_j
\quad \Longleftrightarrow \quad
\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{C}_i, \mathcal{C}_j) \neq 0.
\end{equation}

